      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَاجَةٌ</span></b>  A ewe <i>that does not desire the ram:</i> as
though deprived of excitement. (M.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَاجَةٌ</span>
<i>A female frog.</i> (L, K.) See an ex. in a verse
cited voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صُبَارَةٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <i>An ostrich.</i> (L.) Pl. of
both, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَاجَاتٌ</span>. (L. K.) Dim. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُوَيْجَةٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُيَيْجَةٌ</span>.
(L.)

